# Modelfile — builds the `qwen3.8-coder` FALLBACK driver for Ollama.
#
#   ollama create qwen3.8-coder -f Modelfile
#
# The primary server in this setup is oMLX (see setup.sh / README). Ollama is
# only the fallback: since Ollama 0.32 its llama.cpp runner re-prefills the
# ENTIRE prompt on every request for Qwen 3.5/3.6/3.8 (hybrid Gated-DeltaNet
# attention defeats its prompt cache — "forcing full prompt re-processing due
# to lack of cache data"). For agent workloads that send 20–40k tokens per turn
# this means minutes of time-to-first-token. Use it only if oMLX is unavailable.
#
# Base: the Ollama-library MTP build (Q4_K_M, ~18 GB). MTP = the model's own
# multi-token-prediction head, used by llama.cpp as a lossless speculative
# drafter (~1.4–2x decode speed-up). Needs Ollama 0.34+.
FROM qwen3.8:27b-mtp-q4_K_M

# --- Context window -----------------------------------------------------------
# CRITICAL: Ollama defaults num_ctx to 4096, which silently truncates the system
# prompt + tool schemas and makes tool use fail intermittently with no error.
PARAMETER num_ctx 65536

# --- Sampling (Qwen3.8 model card, thinking mode) -----------------------------
PARAMETER temperature 1.0
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER presence_penalty 0
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.0
